    Certified theorems:

      mirror_lemma_qed :
        compact endpoint bundling full-fixed-point collapse, live mirror
        irrefutability, and coded recognition opacity

      recursive_mirror_lemma_qed :
        compact endpoint bundling coded all-depth recursive opacity in both
        adequate-family and seed-plus-preservation forms

      mirror_opacity :
        a one-way external mirror position in a consistent embedded theory is
        irrefutable and opaque to adequate internal recognition

      external_fixed_point_unconditionally_collapses :
        a full negation fixed point derives `Bot` in the M001 specialization

      external_fixed_point_excludes_checked_refutation_recognition :
        legacy full-fixed-point corollary; the preferred contract uses the
        corresponding external mirror-position theorem

      coded_recursive_mirror_lemma / coded_recursive_mirror_lemma_from_seed :
        the preferred coded all-depth opacity results, respectively from an
        adequate family and from a seed plus a position-preserving mirror step

      logical_operational_recurrence /
      attributed_provenance_operational_recurrence :
        finite recurrence repeats regulated logical content and its concrete
        provenance observation while preserving coded opacity

      externally_attributed_observation_externalizes :
        an operational state explicitly tagged with external provenance
        satisfies the concrete externalization relation

      conditional_externalization_principle :
        `AsIF` entails externalization under an explicit response law

      conditional_attributional_ambiguity_principle :
        both supplied provenance formulas remain irrefutable under an explicit
        ambiguity response law

      fixed_point_certificate_opacity :
        an adequate fixed-point certificate in the regulated position is
        excluded by consistency

      coded_fixed_point_certificate_opacity :
        the concrete finite recognition regulator cannot accept an external
        fixed-point claim in a consistent embedded theory

      incomprehensibility_of_symbolic_regulation :
        compatibility alias only; the broader interpretive reading is not part
        of the certified conclusion

      finite_perpetuity_of_ignorance :
        every adequate finite mirror iterate remains irrefutable and
        recognition-opaque

      paradox_of_the_external :
        an opacity response stabilizes external provenance for the internally
        generated paradox

      symbolic_regulation_qed :
        the complete regulated-assumption and mirror-opacity contract

    Assumption reports are emitted only for `mirror_lemma_qed`,
    `recursive_mirror_lemma_qed`, and `symbolic_regulation_qed`.


7 - Notes
    -----

    `AsIF` denotes non-refutability. Its operational role is continuation under
    an assumption, as provided by the ordinary M001 context rule. Recognition
    adequacy is an explicit re-entry condition on a supplied coding.

    Recursive depth is finite and syntactic. The implication-reflection mirror
    is interderivable with its input, so its iteration validates preservation
    and certificate plumbing but does not by itself create a new semantic
    perspective. Physical recurrence, temporal persistence, and observable
    salience require an interpretation of the formal regulator.

    “Internal Rice-like obstruction” is the intended structural interpretation
    of recognition opacity. L002 does not invoke or certify Rice's theorem. Its
    proved claim is narrower: adequate internal recognition of the supplied
    mirror position would reconstruct its counter-position and contradict
    consistency.

    Mirror irrefutability and coded recognition opacity are certified logical
    results. `AttributedProvenanceOperationalLayer` records literal operational
    attribution tags and supplies a concrete externalization relation. The type
    deliberately does not identify those tags with independently verified
    origins; connecting an attribution to a real system remains empirical.
    Legacy formula-valued attribution response laws remain distinct from truth
    or positive belief.
